# Store LF in the repository and check out LF on every platform.
#
# The paper pins the two upstream companion files (nn_aes.py, utils.py) by a
# line-ending-independent digest: SHA-256 after normalizing CRLF to LF. Forcing
# LF here makes a plain `sha256sum` on a fresh clone reproduce that digest
# directly, on Windows as well as on Linux/macOS, regardless of the cloner's
# core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf
